naga 30.0.1 (crates.io; gfx-rs/wgpu, naga/ at 40f4a34ebaf56f9a046231f54125ad046239d3f3),
SPIR-V backend: the `sample_mask` built-in declared as an array of one
32-bit integer, loaded and stored through its first element, as Vulkan
requires (VUID-SampleMask-SampleMask-04359: "BuiltIn SampleMask variable
needs to be a 32-bit int array"); a scalar was emitted before. Apply in
naga/ with `patch -p1 < ../naga-sample-mask.patch` when moving to a newer
naga that still lacks the fix.

